\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The bounds stay inside the finite inequality}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{The determinant in \ref{fdip-0136} is a product of the
declared diagonal squares with the size correction #{73}.
The lower bound is the inequality of \ref{fdip-0134} on one
basis vector. Neither step uses the maximization of a
quotient on the compact sphere. \ref{fdip-011Y} records that
maximization as the source of the Rayleigh hypothesis, and
\ref{fdip-012P} remains the characteristic polynomial of both
matrices.}
